<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-1911] Discovery MessageWorker thread moves node to &quot;zombie&quot; state when fails</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1911</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;If MessageWorker thread fails by some reason (i.e. because of uncaught exception) it will move a node to &quot;zombie&quot; state. The node will still accept messages through SocketReader but won&apos;t process them. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At some point of time the node will fail because the message queue will be overflowed. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Such a node must be stopped as soon as MessageWorker terminates.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
